        "id": 1308473
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-21T05:44:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for your suggestion. Tried to use TreeMap here but met a problem on sort responses. I spent some time trying to figure the rules out but still couldn\u0027t find the right approach. So I keep using the current ArrayMap design and replace the String with CacheKey.",
      "parentUuid": "8024470b_2b360ce7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 45,
        "startChar": 54,
        "endLine": 45,
        "endChar": 69
      },
      "revId": "9919ec18605830fcf641c98ab36f42e30faf607c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dc4f379f_3d5b0a94",
        "filename": "service-t/src/com/android/server/connectivity/mdns/MdnsServiceCache.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 55,
      "author": {
        "id": 1288034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-15T09:40:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This uses a lock but returns a set of mutable MdnsResponse that could be modified without holding the lock.\n\nAlso it\u0027s confusing that this uses \"this\" as lock, but MdnsServiceTypeClient also has a \"lock\" for other purposes.\n\nIn general I think we avoid locks in core networking code because it brings a lot of difficult problems, and use Handler instead. Do you think you could have a change to make MdnsServiceTypeClient run in a given Handler (at least everything except the QueryTask) ? Basically you\u0027d check the current thread in all public methods. There\u0027s a number of changes needed across MdnsDiscoveryManager and MdnsServiceTypeClient to achieve that I think.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 55,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 55,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "9919ec18605830fcf641c98ab36f42e30faf607c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6c51c5b0_12fe3647",
        "filename": "service-t/src/com/android/server/connectivity/mdns/MdnsServiceCache.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 55,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308473
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-21T05:44:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e This uses a lock but returns a set of mutable MdnsResponse that could be modified without holding the lock.\n\nChange to return a unmodifiableSet.\n\n\u003e Also it\u0027s confusing that this uses \"this\" as lock, but MdnsServiceTypeClient also has a \"lock\" for other purposes.\n\nRemove the lock here by adding the ensureRunningOnHandlerThread() check.\n\n\n\u003e In general I think we avoid locks in core networking code because it brings a lot of difficult problems, and use Handler instead. Do you think you could have a change to make MdnsServiceTypeClient run in a given Handler (at least everything except the QueryTask) ?\n\nI think MdnsServiceTypeClient is already ruuning on handler thread (except the QueryTask) if MdnsDiscoveryManager is running with MdnsMultinetworkSocketClient. If running with MdnsSocketClient, MdnsServiceTypeClient will be accessed from different threads (send/receive). But we don\u0027t use that code now, maybe resolve the problem when upstreaming.\n\n\u003e Basically you\u0027d check the current thread in all public methods. There\u0027s a number of changes needed across MdnsDiscoveryManager and MdnsServiceTypeClient to achieve that I think.\n\nAdd the ensureRunningOnHandlerThread() check to all public methods.",
      "parentUuid": "dc4f379f_3d5b0a94",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 55,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 55,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "9919ec18605830fcf641c98ab36f42e30faf607c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cc918d2c_16946be1",
        "filename": "service-t/src/com/android/server/connectivity/mdns/MdnsServiceCache.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 55,
      "author": {
        "id": 1288034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-21T08:33:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e If running with MdnsSocketClient, MdnsServiceTypeClient will be accessed from different threads (send/receive). But we don\u0027t use that code now, maybe resolve the problem when upstreaming\n\nNoted some comments in the next change, but I think we shouldn\u0027t break the MdnsSocketClient. It is now downstream of this code actually, since there\u0027s a job configured to copy this code over there, and we shouldn\u0027t break it on the next import.",
      "parentUuid": "6c51c5b0_12fe3647",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 55,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 55,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "9919ec18605830fcf641c98ab36f42e30faf607c",
