      "writtenOn": "2023-03-15T08:24:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Considering b/272194544, this should probably use case-insensitive matching.\n\nYou could for example have all keys be lowercase (and query with serviceType converted to lowercase); or you could use a TreeMap with a custom comparator, which would be less memory efficient.\n\nNote that I used CASE_INSENSITIVE_ORDER in the past, but that\u0027s not actually correct: as per the RFC (RFC6762 16. last paragraph), only a-z should be case-insensitive, and I think (?) CASE_INSENSITIVE_ORDER is a bit more generic. If you write some method to convert to lowercase this way, we could reuse it (and write comparators for maps based on it)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 58,
        "startChar": 60,
        "endLine": 58,
        "endChar": 63
      },
      "revId": "9919ec18605830fcf641c98ab36f42e30faf607c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
